WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.230
Let's go!

00:36.450 --> 00:37.680
Um...

00:37.680 --> 00:40.080
So yeah...

00:41.170 --> 00:44.390
since we're both felines, could you?

00:45.030 --> 00:45.840
What are you talking about?

02:20.830 --> 02:23.430
I smell something fried.

02:23.430 --> 02:25.470
Like a croquette or something.

02:25.470 --> 02:28.440
You don't have any croquettes with you by any chance, do you?

02:29.220 --> 02:30.940
What are you jabbering about?

02:30.940 --> 02:34.510
We're about to have a fight to the death here.

02:34.810 --> 02:36.380
Why would I have any croquettes with—

02:36.380 --> 02:39.160
I bet you're hiding them behind your shield.

02:39.160 --> 02:41.040
What a persistent man.

02:41.040 --> 02:42.460
Enough of your chitchat!

02:42.460 --> 02:44.050
See? There's nothing behind it.

02:44.050 --> 02:45.580
Let me see that shield.

02:45.580 --> 02:46.580
U-Um...

02:52.290 --> 02:55.210
What's this in compartment two?

02:55.210 --> 02:56.890
Tokachi croquettes.

02:56.890 --> 02:58.570
And what else?

02:58.570 --> 02:59.520
And deep-fried kebabs.

02:59.520 --> 03:00.960
So you had them after all.

03:00.960 --> 03:01.640
Yes.

03:01.640 --> 03:03.450
What's inside compartment three?

03:03.450 --> 03:05.410
A towel, my cellphone,

03:05.410 --> 03:07.660
some neosporin, and band-aids.

03:07.660 --> 03:08.720
And in compartment one?

03:08.720 --> 03:10.260
That's the key to the base!

03:10.260 --> 03:13.360
Is your shield a freakin' tote bag?!

03:19.730 --> 03:21.190
Home delivery!

03:21.290 --> 03:22.350
Kayoko.

03:22.350 --> 03:23.720
Coming!

03:23.720 --> 03:25.320
What could it be?

03:25.920 --> 03:28.740
Oh, it's probably the nozawana.

03:28.740 --> 03:32.720
Vamp told me he ordered some from this mail order place, so I bought some too.

03:34.450 --> 03:35.830
Thank you.

03:36.370 --> 03:38.110
Nope, it's actually for you.

03:38.660 --> 03:39.370
For me?

03:39.370 --> 03:39.990
What is this thing?

03:41.050 --> 03:42.370
It's a battle suit!

03:45.460 --> 03:47.440
It's cream-colored... are you going for an image change?

03:47.440 --> 03:51.620
This isn't mine, it's actually Tottori Fighter Sakyuun's costume.

03:52.620 --> 03:54.250
Why was it delivered to you, then?

03:54.250 --> 03:56.660
I guess he must have ordered a new one.

03:56.660 --> 03:58.050
Hello?

03:58.050 --> 04:00.540
Oh, the manufacturer must have mistaken our names.

04:00.540 --> 04:01.580
The manufacturer?

04:01.580 --> 04:03.500
I don't really know how to elaborate on it,

04:02.760 --> 04:06.250
"To" comes after "Te" in Japanese phonetical order

04:03.500 --> 04:06.250
but his hero title is alphabetically after mine on the Heroes List:

04:06.250 --> 04:09.390
Astro Fighter and Tottori Fighter.

04:09.390 --> 04:11.670
And then you have our names, Sunred and Sakyuun.

04:11.670 --> 04:13.910
They both start with "S" so it makes it even more confusing.

04:13.910 --> 04:16.960
They actually sent a pair of my boots to his place one time.

04:16.960 --> 04:19.180
You should send it back to him right away, then.

04:22.230 --> 04:23.500
What?

04:23.500 --> 04:24.870
I think I'm going to try it on.

04:25.710 --> 04:27.830
You shouldn't do that, it's not even yours!

04:27.830 --> 04:30.360
We both wear "L" so it should fit.

04:30.360 --> 04:32.700
Battle suits come in "SML" tags?

04:32.700 --> 04:33.890
See, it's a perfect fit!

04:33.890 --> 04:34.790
Actually it's pretty light!

04:34.790 --> 04:37.460
This battle suit's really flexible.

04:37.460 --> 04:40.600
He did say something about it being designed to improve mobility in sand.

04:40.600 --> 04:42.490
I guess that makes sense since he's a Sand Fighter.

04:43.190 --> 04:44.600
It even has his new helmet!

04:45.710 --> 04:47.580
A little loose, but it fits just fine.

04:47.580 --> 04:48.710
Why don't you take it off now?

04:48.710 --> 04:50.370
That <i>is </i> his new costume, you know.

04:50.370 --> 04:51.720
I just had a good idea.

04:52.520 --> 04:55.050
I'm going to play a prank on Vamp with this.

04:56.780 --> 04:58.800
Devil Tentacles!

05:01.150 --> 05:03.570
That sure is a formidable display of strength, Pusogto.

05:03.570 --> 05:07.370
I hereby entrust the next Sunred Obliteration Operation to you.

05:08.570 --> 05:10.570
Stop right there, Florsheim monsters!

05:10.570 --> 05:11.260
What?

05:13.330 --> 05:14.860
Who are you?

05:14.860 --> 05:17.740
I'm the one who's going to take you down!

05:17.740 --> 05:19.610
Tottori Fighter Sakyuun

05:19.610 --> 05:20.760
has arrived!

05:22.390 --> 05:26.250
Tottori Fighter Sakyuun is a well known fighter from the Tottori Prefecture.

05:26.250 --> 05:27.650
Being the Sand Fighter he is,

05:27.650 --> 05:30.460
he uses Mother Earth's powers to defeat the forces of evil!

05:30.860 --> 05:31.590
Tottori?

05:31.590 --> 05:34.140
W-Why is a fighter from Tottori in Kanagawa?

05:34.140 --> 05:35.240
Here I come,

05:35.240 --> 05:36.740
Sakyuun Jump!

05:37.340 --> 05:38.470
Interesting.

05:38.470 --> 05:41.000
You'll be a nice warm up to fighting Sunred.

05:41.000 --> 05:42.210
Kill him!

05:42.210 --> 05:44.520
Sakyuun Javelin!

05:45.050 --> 05:47.130
Devil Tentacles!

05:52.660 --> 05:54.280
Ah shit, the helmet slipped out of place!

05:54.280 --> 05:57.140
Black Dream!

05:58.090 --> 05:58.940
What the hell is this?

06:00.660 --> 06:01.450
Now's the chance!

06:01.450 --> 06:03.800
Take him down now, Pusogto!

06:03.800 --> 06:05.600
Crap, I'm borrowing this without his permission too.

06:05.600 --> 06:06.880
I gotta wash this right away.

06:09.850 --> 06:11.790
W-What just happened?

06:12.190 --> 06:14.230
Did he just run away?

06:14.230 --> 06:15.290
Maybe?

06:19.610 --> 06:21.450
You are such an idiot.

06:21.450 --> 06:23.960
Those guys were way too into it.

06:23.960 --> 06:25.150
But thank god.

06:25.150 --> 06:26.550
I don't know if they just make detergent extra strong these days

06:26.550 --> 06:28.930
or if that guy's ink doesn't stain all that well,

06:28.930 --> 06:30.440
but all the stains came out.

06:30.440 --> 06:31.350
All right.

06:31.350 --> 06:33.980
Once we iron this baby, he won't notice a thing.

06:33.980 --> 06:36.620
Do me a favor and tell Sakyuun you don't know anything

06:36.620 --> 06:38.790
if he notices, so we have our stories straight.

06:38.790 --> 06:40.030
No way!

06:40.030 --> 06:42.810
You call yourself a <i>Hero </i> and you're telling me to <i>lie </i>?

06:42.810 --> 06:43.400
Well...

06:43.400 --> 06:45.160
You're on your own, mister.

06:45.160 --> 06:47.440
I'm going to tell him the truth if he asks me about it.

06:47.440 --> 06:48.490
Fine.

06:48.490 --> 06:51.700
Then just don't answer the phone if he calls, okay?

06:53.270 --> 06:55.640
Oh man,

06:55.640 --> 06:58.360
you really should have been there, Mr. Red.

06:58.360 --> 07:00.780
You could have seen our new and improved powers.

07:00.780 --> 07:04.610
Oh I know very well how "new and improved" your powers are.

07:04.610 --> 07:07.210
Sakyuun was really strong,

07:07.210 --> 07:09.700
but he wasn't a match for us.

07:09.700 --> 07:12.660
You would have completely beaten him with your next attack, right?

07:13.360 --> 07:14.560
Yeah, probably.

07:14.560 --> 07:18.820
I think that the first Devil Tentacle attack you did actually hit him.

07:18.820 --> 07:20.280
Yeah, I thought so too.

07:20.280 --> 07:21.270
Yeah, right.

07:21.270 --> 07:24.490
That's probably why he couldn't dodge your Black Dream attack!

07:24.490 --> 07:26.330
It never hit me, damn it.

07:26.330 --> 07:28.220
He probably broke one of his shoulders after that.

07:28.220 --> 07:30.440
That was all just the helmet falling out of place.

07:30.440 --> 07:33.280
But wasn't Sakyuun awesome too?

07:33.280 --> 07:34.900
Now he's what you call a Hero.

07:34.900 --> 07:36.130
He even used a weapon!

07:36.130 --> 07:38.580
He did this flashy move when he was dodging my attacks too!

07:38.580 --> 07:41.160
That's the kind of fights I've been wanting to see.

07:41.160 --> 07:42.280
Right there!

07:42.280 --> 07:45.240
We're good at fights like those.

07:45.240 --> 07:46.360
Right?

07:46.360 --> 07:48.780
He even ran away in the end.

07:48.780 --> 07:51.090
Didn't it really pump you up?

07:51.090 --> 07:52.980
I think it's actually brought me luck!

07:52.980 --> 07:56.760
I'm really looking forward to our next fight with Mr. Red now.

07:56.760 --> 07:59.280
You better watch out, Mr. Red.

08:02.780 --> 08:03.920
I'm home.

08:03.920 --> 08:05.210
Kayoko!

08:05.210 --> 08:07.560
Oh, nice for you to come over, Vamp.

08:07.560 --> 08:09.070
I brought over the nozawana we ordered.

08:09.970 --> 08:12.650
I figured shipping would be more expensive if we ordered it separately,

08:12.650 --> 08:15.110
so I had them deliver both over to our place.

08:15.110 --> 08:17.190
I expected no less from you, Vamp!

08:20.300 --> 08:22.470
Did you go somewhere during the long weekend?

08:22.470 --> 08:24.030
Yeah, I went to Tokyo Bay.

08:24.030 --> 08:25.720
Tokyo Bay, huh?

08:27.120 --> 08:29.290
Look at that, Pusogto!

08:29.290 --> 08:31.110
Hey Sakyuun!

08:32.250 --> 08:33.930
Long time no see, man.

08:33.930 --> 08:34.830
How've you been?

08:34.830 --> 08:35.970
What are you up to?

08:35.970 --> 08:38.830
So I guess you didn't go back to Tottori yet.

08:39.820 --> 08:41.500
Why are you being all quiet?

08:41.500 --> 08:44.090
You're acting like you've never seen us before, man.

08:44.090 --> 08:46.220
Did you not have enough after losing last time?

08:46.220 --> 08:47.890
Wait,

08:47.890 --> 08:49.930
could it be you were so pissed about it that you couldn't go home?

08:49.930 --> 08:52.700
I'll lay you out like an octopus if you keep talking nonsense like that, punk.

08:54.270 --> 08:54.810
What?

08:54.810 --> 08:56.720
Did you just say something?

08:56.720 --> 08:58.650
You didn't just tell an octopus that you'll lay it out like an octopus, did you?

08:58.650 --> 09:00.320
You got quite a mouth on you, huh?

09:00.320 --> 09:01.420
Yeah, after running away last time, too.

09:01.420 --> 09:03.570
I'd love to see you try!

09:03.570 --> 09:04.660
Avas—

09:04.660 --> 09:05.890
Small fry.

09:09.140 --> 09:11.810
Sorry I had you come all the way here, Sakyuun.

09:11.810 --> 09:14.960
It's okay, I figured I wanted to see you anyway, Red.

09:15.160 --> 09:16.990
Here's your battle suit.

09:16.990 --> 09:18.200
I'm so sorry about this.

09:18.200 --> 09:21.670
That manufacturer really needs to get his head straight, huh?

09:21.670 --> 09:22.340
Oh yeah,

09:22.340 --> 09:26.560
I ran into this weird octopus guy who kept trying to pick a fight on my way here.

09:28.160 --> 09:30.580
Oh yeah, we get those weird idiots over here sometimes.

09:30.580 --> 09:31.830
Just ignore them.

09:31.830 --> 09:34.410
I gave him a little taste of hell though.

09:34.410 --> 09:35.740
I feel so bad for you!

09:35.740 --> 09:38.330
You shouldn't have to be fighting those types of monsters!

09:38.330 --> 09:40.610
I-I guess...

10:04.000 --> 10:04.770
Maybe.

10:08.940 --> 10:09.950
안녕하세요?

10:10.540 --> 10:13.450
It's time for General Vamp's Quick Cooking.

10:13.450 --> 10:15.220
Our menu this time is:

10:15.920 --> 10:18.220
a Korean Raw Egg Bowl.

10:18.220 --> 10:22.130
You'll like it since it's a little different from your average raw egg bowl.

10:22.630 --> 10:24.720
And your ingredients are:

10:24.720 --> 10:26.900
a bowl of rice,

10:26.900 --> 10:28.410
a raw egg,

10:28.410 --> 10:31.990
some sesame oil, nori, and soy sauce.

10:32.590 --> 10:34.140
Let's get right to the cooking.

10:34.140 --> 10:38.760
First make a small crater on the warm rice using your chopsticks.

10:38.760 --> 10:42.970
This way you can put the egg on top without spilling it.

10:42.970 --> 10:45.770
Next pour some sesame oil over the rice,

10:45.770 --> 10:49.030
tear up the nori into small pieces and put those on top of the rice too.

10:49.030 --> 10:52.000
You can put as much nori as you like.

10:52.000 --> 10:55.230
After that, we need to separate the yolk from the whites.

10:55.230 --> 10:58.100
Roll the egg in your hands like a hot potato

10:58.100 --> 11:00.990
will make separating the yolk a cinch.

11:00.990 --> 11:02.860
Let's challenge!

11:02.860 --> 11:05.020
Put the egg yolk on top of the rice,

11:05.020 --> 11:07.710
topping it all off with a little bit of soy sauce...

11:08.710 --> 11:10.920
and you're done already!

11:10.920 --> 11:13.300
Voila, a Korean Raw Egg Bowl.

11:13.300 --> 11:15.270
Remember to mix well before eating.

11:15.270 --> 11:19.760
Using sukiyaki sauce instead of soy sauce gives it a deeper flavor too.

11:19.760 --> 11:21.740
It seems like this would come in handy when I'm a little hungry

11:21.740 --> 11:23.650
since it's so easy to make.

11:23.650 --> 11:25.140
Be sure to save the egg whites

11:25.140 --> 11:27.860
and use it when you're making instant seaweed soup or something.

11:27.860 --> 11:29.900
You shouldn't just toss it and let it go to waste!
